('57a145db-e4b2-514f-abee-e842e477efa9','ad0636e5-7484-582c-89af-fa3ab098bfef',1,'possibility','امکان','spoken & written','the possibility that something will happen, especially something you want','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'شانس، امکان؛ فرصت؛ تصادف','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have/stand a chance (of something) (= it is possible you will do it ) I think you have a good chance of getting the job.','give somebody a chance of doing something (= say how likely it is that they will do it ) He has been given a fifty-fifty chance of being fit for Sunday’s match.','increase the chance of something Certain foods increase the chance of heart disease.','improve the chance of something The book shows you how to improve your chance of success.','reduce/lessen the chance of something The talks were aimed at reducing the chance of war.','ruin any chance of something (= make it impossible for something to happen ) Drinking alcohol can ruin any chance of weight loss.','jeopardize any chance of something (= make something less likely to happen ) This could jeopardize any chance of a ceasefire.','a good chance (= when something is likely ) I think there is a good chance that he will say yes.','every chance (= a good chance ) There’s every chance that the baby will survive.','some chance There’s some chance of snow later this week.','a small/slight/slim chance He only has a very small chance of being elected. There’s a slight chance of some sunshine in the west.','no/little/not much chance The prisoners knew there was little chance of escape.','a one in three/four/ten etc chance (= used to say how likely something is ) People in their 30s have a one in 3,000 chance of getting the disease.','a fair chance (= a fairly good chance ) If you work, you have a fair chance of passing the test.','a sporting chance (= a fairly good chance ) The proposals had at least a sporting chance of being accepted.','a fighting chance (= a small but real chance ) The Republican Party has a fighting chance at the next election.','a fifty-fifty chance (= an equal chance that something will or will not happen ) I’d say there is a 50–50 chance that the deal will go through.','an outside/a remote chance (= a very small chance ) He still has an outside chance of winning the championship.','a million-to-one chance/a one in a million chance (= when something is extremely unlikely ) It must have been a million-to-one chance that we’d meet.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There’s always the chance that something will go wrong.","translation":"همیشه این احتمال وجود دارد که مشکلی پیش بیاید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001940174.mp3"},{"sentence":"What are the team’s chances of success?","translation":"شانس موفقیت تیم چقدر است؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001069239.mp3"},{"sentence":"If we did move to London, I’d stand a much better chance (= have a much better chance ) of getting a job.","translation":"اگر ما به لندن نقل مکان می‌کردیم، شانس بیشتری (= شانس بهتری) برای یافتن شغل داشتم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001069282.mp3"},{"sentence":"There is little chance of her being found alive.","translation":"احتمال کمی وجود دارد که او زنده پیدا شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001940181.mp3"},{"sentence":"Chances are (= it is likely that ) you’ll be fine.","translation":"به احتمال زیاد (= این احتمال وجود دارد که) خوب باشید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000283.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('41760602-5d7b-5327-a4a6-05adcd1686ab','ad0636e5-7484-582c-89af-fa3ab098bfef',2,'opportunity','فرصت','spoken & written','a time or situation which you can use to do something that you want to do','[ countable ]',null,'زمان یا موقعیتی که می توانید برای انجام کاری که می خواهید انجام دهید از آن استفاده کنید',array['opportunity']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Ralph was waiting for a chance to introduce himself.","translation":"رالف منتظر فرصتی بود تا خود را معرفی کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001069332.mp3"},{"sentence":"our only chance of escape","translation":"تنها شانس ما برای فرار","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001069335.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’m sorry, I haven’t had a chance to look at it yet.","translation":"متاسفم، من هنوز فرصتی برای نگاه کردن به آن نداشتم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001687530.mp3"},{"sentence":"If someone invited me over to Florida, I’d jump at the chance (= use the opportunity eagerly ) .","translation":"اگر کسی من را به فلوریدا دعوت کند، از فرصت استفاده می‌کنم (= از این فرصت مشتاقانه استفاده می‌کنم).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001069349.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('47f4e041-a265-5da4-9aa6-2ab8e8f45f91','ad0636e5-7484-582c-89af-fa3ab098bfef',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'take a chance','شانس، امکان؛ فرصت؛ تصادف','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('bbb601e9-0347-563d-a35b-1000a67b8677','ad0636e5-7484-582c-89af-fa3ab098bfef',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'somebody’s chances','شانس، امکان؛ فرصت؛ تصادف','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('f2c584f8-35fd-5e45-8d1b-138adeded60a','ad0636e5-7484-582c-89af-fa3ab098bfef',5,'luck','شانس','spoken & written','the way some things happen without being planned or caused by people','[ uncountable ]',null,'روشی که بعضی چیزها بدون برنامه ریزی یا ایجاد شده توسط افراد اتفاق می افتد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I bumped into her quite by chance in Oxford Street.","translation":"من کاملاً تصادفی در خیابان آکسفورد به او برخورد کردم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001069399.mp3"},{"sentence":"Dave had thought of every possibility, he was leaving nothing to chance.","translation":"دیو به هر احتمالی فکر کرده بود، او هیچ چیز را به شانس واگذار نمی کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001687577.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was pure chance that they ended up working in the same office in the same town.","translation":"این شانس محض بود که آنها در یک دفتر در همان شهر کار کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001069403.mp3"},{"sentence":"As chance would have it , the one time I wanted to see her, she wasn’t in.","translation":"به احتمال زیاد، یک بار که می خواستم او را ببینم، او در آنجا نبود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001069407.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
