('aa47d21e-08e2-5548-9611-abd4bf2ec5cd','b9936d2c-84d5-52fc-9dff-ab92c1f71bff',1,'things becoming different','چیزها متفاوت می شوند','spoken & written','the process or result of something or someone becoming different','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'تغییر، دگرگونی؛ باقی‌مانده (پول)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['big/major Going to a new school is a big change for children.','slight/small/minor The proposed changes were relatively minor.','gradual There has been a gradual change in the weather.','dramatic/drastic/radical (= very big, especially in way that is surprising ) The Industrial Revolution was a period of dramatic change.','significant The change in blood pressure was not significant.','marked (= very noticeable ) There was a marked change in his behaviour.','fundamental Reducing waste requires a fundamental change in attitude.','social/political/economic etc change Demands for political and social change are growing.','sweeping changes (= affecting many things or people, especially because of an official decision ) There are likely to be sweeping changes in the company.','far-reaching changes (= important and having a great effect that will last a long time ) The Internet has brought about far-reaching changes in the way we work.','make a change We''ve had to make some changes to the design.','introduce a change A number of changes were introduced to the curriculum.','bring (about) change ( also effect a change formal ) (= cause change ) The war brought about radical social change. Treatment is aimed at effecting a change in the child’s negative behaviour.','see/notice/observe a change I saw a big change in her when I met her again.','undergo a change (= be affected by a change ) The body undergoes a number of changes during this time.','signal a change (= be a sign of a change ) Does this move signal a change in US foreign policy?','the pace/rate of change People sometimes feel alarmed by the pace of technological change.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I find it hard to cope with change.","translation":"کنار آمدن با تغییر برای من سخت است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001071076.mp3"},{"sentence":"scientists worried about climatic change","translation":"دانشمندان نگران تغییرات آب و هوایی هستند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001667140.mp3"},{"sentence":"changes in the immigration laws","translation":"تغییرات در قوانین مهاجرت","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001071075.mp3"},{"sentence":"A change in personality may mean your teenager has a drug problem.","translation":"تغییر در شخصیت ممکن است به این معنی باشد که نوجوان شما مشکل مواد مخدر دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001071074.mp3"},{"sentence":"a change of temperature","translation":"تغییر دما","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001071079.mp3"},{"sentence":"No major changes were made to the book.","translation":"هیچ تغییر اساسی در کتاب ایجاد نشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001667141.mp3"},{"sentence":"There was a change for the better in the patient’s condition.","translation":"در وضعیت بیمار تغییری برای بهتر شدن وجود داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001071083.mp3"},{"sentence":"the sweeping political changes after the First World War","translation":"تغییرات سیاسی گسترده پس از جنگ جهانی اول","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001667147.mp3"},{"sentence":"She had a change of heart (= change in attitude ) and decided to stay.","translation":"او تغییر قلب (= تغییر در نگرش) داشت و تصمیم گرفت بماند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001071087.mp3"},{"sentence":"Family life has undergone dramatic change in recent years.","translation":"زندگی خانوادگی در سال های اخیر دستخوش تغییرات چشمگیری شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001667151.mp3"}]'::jsonb,10),
('5ab582b5-ab8c-5462-8894-90c3b4bf7aa0','b9936d2c-84d5-52fc-9dff-ab92c1f71bff',2,'from one thing to another','از یک چیز به چیز دیگر','spoken & written','the fact of one thing or person being replaced by another','[ countable ]',null,'این واقعیت که یک چیز یا شخص با چیز دیگری جایگزین می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['big/major Going to a new school is a big change for children.','slight/small/minor The proposed changes were relatively minor.','gradual There has been a gradual change in the weather.','dramatic/drastic/radical (= very big, especially in way that is surprising ) The Industrial Revolution was a period of dramatic change.','significant The change in blood pressure was not significant.','marked (= very noticeable ) There was a marked change in his behaviour.','fundamental Reducing waste requires a fundamental change in attitude.','social/political/economic etc change Demands for political and social change are growing.','sweeping changes (= affecting many things or people, especially because of an official decision ) There are likely to be sweeping changes in the company.','far-reaching changes (= important and having a great effect that will last a long time ) The Internet has brought about far-reaching changes in the way we work.','make a change We''ve had to make some changes to the design.','introduce a change A number of changes were introduced to the curriculum.','bring (about) change ( also effect a change formal ) (= cause change ) The war brought about radical social change. Treatment is aimed at effecting a change in the child’s negative behaviour.','see/notice/observe a change I saw a big change in her when I met her again.','undergo a change (= be affected by a change ) The body undergoes a number of changes during this time.','signal a change (= be a sign of a change ) Does this move signal a change in US foreign policy?','the pace/rate of change People sometimes feel alarmed by the pace of technological change.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The car needs an oil change.","translation":"ماشین نیاز به تعویض روغن دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001071101.mp3"},{"sentence":"a change of government","translation":"تغییر حکومت","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001071096.mp3"},{"sentence":"a change of address","translation":"تغییر آدرس","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001071097.mp3"},{"sentence":"the gradual change from grasslands to true desert","translation":"تغییر تدریجی از علفزار به بیابان واقعی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001071100.mp3"},{"sentence":"The government has made some major policy changes .","translation":"دولت تغییرات عمده ای در سیاست ایجاد کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001667160.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('2bdc1df9-0540-5a78-9aba-04dbdf97645d','b9936d2c-84d5-52fc-9dff-ab92c1f71bff',3,'pleasant new situation','وضعیت جدید دلپذیر','spoken & written','a situation or experience that is different from what happened before, and is usually interesting or enjoyable','[ singular ]',null,'موقعیت یا تجربه ای که با آنچه قبلا اتفاق افتاده متفاوت است و معمولاً جالب یا لذت بخش است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['big/major Going to a new school is a big change for children.','slight/small/minor The proposed changes were relatively minor.','gradual There has been a gradual change in the weather.','dramatic/drastic/radical (= very big, especially in way that is surprising ) The Industrial Revolution was a period of dramatic change.','significant The change in blood pressure was not significant.','marked (= very noticeable ) There was a marked change in his behaviour.','fundamental Reducing waste requires a fundamental change in attitude.','social/political/economic etc change Demands for political and social change are growing.','sweeping changes (= affecting many things or people, especially because of an official decision ) There are likely to be sweeping changes in the company.','far-reaching changes (= important and having a great effect that will last a long time ) The Internet has brought about far-reaching changes in the way we work.','make a change We''ve had to make some changes to the design.','introduce a change A number of changes were introduced to the curriculum.','bring (about) change ( also effect a change formal ) (= cause change ) The war brought about radical social change. Treatment is aimed at effecting a change in the child’s negative behaviour.','see/notice/observe a change I saw a big change in her when I met her again.','undergo a change (= be affected by a change ) The body undergoes a number of changes during this time.','signal a change (= be a sign of a change ) Does this move signal a change in US foreign policy?','the pace/rate of change People sometimes feel alarmed by the pace of technological change.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The morning was cool; a welcome change from the heat of the day before.","translation":"صبح خنک بود. یک تغییر خوشایند نسبت به گرمای روز قبل.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001667167.mp3"},{"sentence":"How about dinner out for a change?","translation":"در مورد شام بیرون برای تغییر چطور؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001071113.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘Ron’s buying the drinks.’ ‘That makes a change.’","translation":"«ران در حال خرید نوشیدنی‌ها است.» «این باعث تغییر می‌شود.»","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001071117.mp3"},{"sentence":"The patients benefit greatly from a change of scenery.","translation":"بیماران از تغییر منظره بسیار سود می برند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001071121.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
