nsumer credit has risen substantially during this period.','interest-free credit (= with no interest added to it ) We offer interest-free credit for up to 50 weeks.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The company promised to provide credits to customers who had been charged too much.","translation":"این شرکت قول داده است که به مشتریانی که بیش از حد هزینه دریافت کرده اند اعتبار ارائه کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001710527.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('70ad20c0-1b4f-5fc5-bd5b-47d227cf518f','bfedf48d-2271-59a8-8487-cb109ac75b9e',11,'true/correct','درست/درست','spoken & written','the belief that something is true or correct','[ uncountable ]',null,'باور به اینکه چیزی درست یا درست است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['buy/get something on credit They bought all their furniture on credit.','use credit The survey showed only 15% of people had never used credit.','get/obtain credit (= be allowed to buy something on credit ) The economic situation is making it more difficult for people to get credit.','give/offer credit (= allow customers to buy things on credit ) A business may lose customers if it does not give credit.','refuse somebody credit You may be refused credit if you have a bad financial record.','a credit card (= a plastic card that you use to buy things and pay for them later ) Can I pay by credit card?','credit facilities (= the opportunity to buy something on credit ) Credit facilities are available if you are over 18.','a credit agreement (= an arrangement to allow or receive credit ) People sometimes sign credit agreements and then realize they can’t afford the payments.','credit terms (= how much you must pay back and when ) The credit terms were a deposit of £1,000 and two later instalments of £900.','somebody’s credit rating (= how likely a bank etc thinks someone is to pay their debts ) If you have a poor credit rating, you will have a hard time getting a mortgage.','a credit risk (= a risk that a bank etc may not get back the money it lends ) Banks first have to assess whether a borrower is a credit risk.','a credit limit (= the most someone can spend using credit ) I have a Visa card with a £1,000 credit limit.','a credit crunch/squeeze (= a situation in which people are not allowed as much credit as before ) Due to a credit squeeze, interest rates rose.','consumer credit (= the amount of credit used by consumers ) Consumer credit has risen substantially during this period.','interest-free credit (= with no interest added to it ) We offer interest-free credit for up to 50 weeks.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The witness’s story gained credit with the jury.","translation":"داستان شاهد مورد توجه هیئت منصفه قرار گرفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001710529.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('91b9aa96-8bcd-55be-a7e7-deebccfe7b3b','1c5ac4d6-5215-5a45-a496-d6f3f57f2e78',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to add money to a bank account',null,null,'برای اضافه کردن پول به حساب بانکی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The cheque has been credited to your account.","translation":"چک به حساب شما واریز شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000845473.mp3"},{"sentence":"For some reason my account’s been credited with an extra $76.","translation":"به دلایلی به حساب من 76 دلار اضافی اعتبار داده شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001710179.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('40d76d0b-04f4-52aa-9ea9-bcb542f4a75f','1c5ac4d6-5215-5a45-a496-d6f3f57f2e78',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'credit somebody with (doing) something',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('cd683bd7-e9ec-5e49-a6b2-7e8dba576c68','1c5ac4d6-5215-5a45-a496-d6f3f57f2e78',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be credited to somebody/something',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('e0dcf015-ad6c-5d1b-9d51-46b26fc42a27','1c5ac4d6-5215-5a45-a496-d6f3f57f2e78',4,null,null,'formal','to believe that something is true',null,null,'باور کردن به اینکه چیزی درست است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We found his statement hard to credit.","translation":"اعتبار اظهارات او برای ما سخت بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000845467.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('defebd41-6f6a-536e-94c0-231e1ebb1bbb','c8bdeaea-c5f1-5de1-b0c9-8e8bce532366',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a situation in which there are a lot of problems that must be dealt with quickly so that the situation does not get worse or more dangerous',null,null,'بحران، دوران سرنوشت‌ساز','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['an economic/political/financial etc crisis The country was headed into an economic crisis.','a constitutional crisis (= relating to the way a country is governed ) The scandal caused the greatest constitutional crisis of modern times.','a major/serious/deep/severe crisis Our farming industry has been hit by a serious crisis.','a worsening/deepening crisis The strikes came during a worsening economic crisis.','create/cause/provoke a crisis The people fled the country, creating a huge refugee crisis.','precipitate a crisis formal (= start one ) The rising oil prices precipitated an energy crisis.','face a crisis Many families are facing a debt crisis.','resolve/overcome a crisis (= deal with it so that it no longer exists ) We still hope that the hostage crisis can be resolved by negotiation.','handle a crisis (= deal with one ) Can he handle the crisis in our prisons?','defuse a crisis (= stop it developing further ) Diplomatic efforts to defuse the crisis have failed.','avert a crisis (= stop it happening ) More talks were proposed in an attempt to avert the crisis.','a debt/food/housing etc crisis The failure of the crop this year will create a food crisis.','a cash crisis (= a lack of money ) In April the company sold another 30% of its stock to ease its cash crisis.','an energy/oil/fuel crisis There is an energy crisis here, with power cuts happening daily.','crisis management (= dealing with a crisis ) Most of my job consists of crisis management.','crisis point (= the point at which a problem becomes a crisis ) Events were now reaching crisis point.','a crisis situation Emergency powers were needed to deal with the crisis situation.','crisis talks (= discussions about a crisis ) The Prime Minister went back to London for crisis talks.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The country now faces an economic crisis .","translation":"اکنون کشور با بحران اقتصادی مواجه است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756043.mp3"},{"sentence":"The prime minister was criticized for the way in which he handled the crisis .","translation":"نخست وزیر به دلیل نحوه مدیریت بحران مورد انتقاد قرار گرفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756046.mp3"},{"sentence":"the current debt crisis","translation":"بحران بدهی فعلی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001842041.mp3"},{"sentence":"a major political crisis","translation":"یک بحران سیاسی بزرگ","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756042.mp3"},{"sentence":"I was relieved that we had averted yet another financial crisis .","translation":"خیالم راحت شد که از یک بحران مالی دیگر جلوگیری کردیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001842042.mp3"},{"sentence":"Oil companies were heavily criticized when they made large profits during the oil crisis of the 1970s.","translation":"شرکت های نفتی زمانی که در جریان بحران نفتی دهه 1970 به سودهای کلان دست یافتند، به شدت مورد انتقاد قرار گرفتند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756054.mp3"},{"sentence":"The car industry is now in crisis .","translation":"صنعت خودرو در حال حاضر در بحران است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756057.mp3"},{"sentence":"He doesn’t seem to be very good at crisis management .","translation":"به نظر نمی رسد که او در مدیریت بحران خیلی خوب باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756047.mp3"}]'::jsonb,8),
('bee28635-f0da-5c7e-9faf-d803f75af0d6','c8bdeaea-c5f1-5de1-b0c9-8e8bce532366',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a time when a personal emotional problem or situation has reached its worst point',null,null,'زمانی که یک مشکل یا موقعیت احساسی شخصی به بدترین نقطه خود رسیده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['an economic/political/financial etc crisis The country was headed into an economic crisis.','a constitutional crisis (= relating to the way a country is governed ) The scandal caused the greatest constitutional crisis of modern times.','a major/serious/deep/severe crisis Our farming industry has been hit by a serious crisis.','a worsening/deepening crisis The strikes came during a worsening economic crisis.','create/cause/provoke a crisis The people fled the country, creating a huge refugee crisis.','precipitate a crisis formal (= start one ) The rising oil prices precipitated an energy crisis.','face a crisis Many families are facing a debt crisis.','resolve/overcome a crisis (= deal with it so that it no longer exists ) We still hope that the hostage crisis can be resolved by negotiation.','handle a crisis (= deal with one ) Can he handle the crisis in our prisons?','defuse a crisis (= stop it developing further ) Diplomatic efforts to defuse the crisis have failed.','avert a crisis (= stop it happening ) More talks were proposed in an attempt to avert the crisis.','a debt/food/housing etc crisis The failure of the crop this year will create a food crisis.','a cash crisis (= a lack of money ) In April the company sold another 30% of its stock to ease its cash crisis.','an energy/oil/fuel crisis There is an energy crisis here, with power cuts happening daily.','crisis management (= dealing with a crisis ) Most of my job consists of crisis management.','crisis point (= the point at which a problem becomes a crisis ) Events were now reaching crisis point.','a crisis situation Emergency powers were needed to deal with the crisis situation.','crisis talks (= discussions about a crisis ) The Prime Minister went back to London for crisis talks.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"an emotional crisis","translation":"یک بحران عاطفی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001842058.mp3"},{"sentence":"In times of crisis, you find out who your real friends are.","translation":"در مواقع بحران، متوجه می شوید که دوستان واقعی شما چه کسانی هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000846665.mp3"},{"sentence":"He seems to be going through a crisis .","translation":"به نظر می رسد او در حال عبور از یک بحران است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756058.mp3"},{"sentence":"She has reached a crisis point in her career.","translation":"او در زندگی حرفه ای خود به نقطه بحرانی رسیده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756064.mp3"},{"sentence":"Both parties experienced an identity crisis (= feeling of uncertainty about their purpose ) at the end of the ''90s.","translation":"هر دو طرف یک بحران هویت (= احساس عدم اطمینان در مورد هدف خود) را در پایان دهه 90 تجربه کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001842059.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('259ba3b5-6d53-5f3a-9f89-67e8d6927e28','c8bdeaea-c5f1-5de1-b0c9-8e8bce532366',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'crisis of confidence','بحران، دوران سرنوشت‌ساز','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['an economic/political/financial etc crisis The country was headed into an economic crisis.','a constitutional crisis (= relating to the way a country is governed ) The scandal caused the greatest constitutional crisis of modern times.','a major/serious/deep/severe crisis Our farming industry has been hit by a serious crisis.','a worsening/deepening crisis The strikes came during a worsening economic crisis.','create/cause/provoke a crisis The people fled the country, creating a huge refugee crisis.','precipitate a crisis formal (= start one ) The rising oil prices precipitated an energy crisis.','face a crisis Many families are facing a debt crisis.','resolve/overcome a crisis (= deal with it so that it no longer exists ) We still hope that the hostage crisis can be resolved by negotiation.','handle a crisis (= deal with one ) Can he handle the crisis in our prisons?','defuse a crisis (= stop it developing further ) Diplomatic efforts to defuse the crisis have failed.','avert a crisis (= stop it happening ) More talks were proposed in an attempt to avert the crisis.','a debt/food/housing etc crisis The failure of the crop this year will create a food crisis.','a cash crisis (= a lack of money ) In April the company sold another 30% of its stock to ease its cash crisis.','an energy/oil/fuel crisis There is an energy crisis here, with power cuts happening daily.','crisis management (= dealing with a crisis ) Most of my job consists of crisis management.','crisis point (= the point at which a problem becomes a crisis ) Events were now reaching crisis point.','a crisis situation Emergency powers were needed to deal with the crisis situation.','crisis talks (= discussions about a crisis ) The Prime Minister went back to London for crisis talks.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('ac19e204-d52e-559e-93c5-3736db7cbe0e','c8bdeaea-c5f1-5de1-b0c9-8e8bce532366',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'crisis of conscience','بحران، دوران سرنوشت‌ساز','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['an economic/political/financial etc crisis The country was headed into an economic crisis.','a constitutional crisis (= relating to the way a country is governed ) The scandal caused the greatest constitutional crisis of modern times.','a major/serious/deep/severe crisis Our farming industry has been hit by a serious crisis.','a worsening/deepening crisis The strikes came during a worsening economic crisis.','create/cause/provoke a crisis The people fled the country, creating a huge refugee crisis.','precipitate a crisis formal (= start one ) The rising oil prices precipitated an energy crisis.','face a crisis Many families are facing a debt crisis.','resolve/overcome a crisis (= deal with it so that it no longer exists ) We still hope that the hostage crisis can be resolved by negotiation.','handle a crisis (= deal with one ) Can he handle the crisis in our prisons?','defuse a crisis (= stop it developing further ) Diplomatic efforts to defuse the crisis have failed.','avert a crisis (= stop it happening ) More talks were proposed in an attempt to avert the crisis.','a debt/food/housing etc crisis The failure of the crop this year will create a food crisis.','a cash crisis (= a lack of money ) In April the company sold another 30% of its stock to ease its cash crisis.','an energy/oil/fuel crisis There is an energy crisis here, with power cuts happening daily.','crisis management (= dealing with a crisis ) Most of my job consists of crisis management.','crisis point (= the point at which a problem becomes a crisis ) Events were now reaching crisis point.','a crisis situation Emergency powers were needed to deal with the crisis situation.','crisis talks (= discussions about a crisis ) The Prime Minister went back to London for crisis talks.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('fbf1034a-9e28-5b28-88e4-0f0eb1e88ef3','a2ed1598-c130-5e86-956c-e0697fdd7582',1,null,null,'spoken & written','someone whose job is to make judgments about the good and bad qualities of art , music , films etc',null,null,'نقدگرا، منتقد؛ منتقدان (هنر/سینما)',array['reviewer']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a film/art/music etc critic He became the chief music critic for the Herald Tribune.','a literary critic (= of books and other literature )','a theatre critic British English , a theater critic American English (= of plays )','a restaurant critic (= of the food, service etc in restaurants ) Being a restaurant critic sounds like a glamorous lifestyle.','a social critic (= of human society and its organizations ) Social critics have argued that television viewing decreases people''s other social activities.','a critic attacks something Many critics attacked Seurat’s paintings for their lack of colour.','a critic praises something The play was highly praised by critics and the public.','a critic hails something/somebody as something (= describes someone or something as very good ) Critics hailed the film as a brilliant portrayal of American society at that time.','a critic pans something ( also a critic slates something British English ) (= criticizes something strongly ) The television series has been panned by critics.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a review by the theatre critic of the ‘Sunday Times’","translation":"نقد منتقد تئاتر «ساندی تایمز»","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756112.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('f94d2400-11e3-5f81-bfb0-a8c5a2393d89','a2ed1598-c130-5e86-956c-e0697fdd7582',2,null,null,'spoken & written','someone who criticizes a person, organization , or idea',null,null,'کسی که از یک شخص، سازمان یا ایده انتقاد می کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a film/art/music etc critic He became the chief music critic for the Herald Tribune.','a literary critic (= of books and other literature )','a theatre critic British English , a theater critic American English (= of plays )','a restaurant critic (= of the food, service etc in restaurants ) Being a restaurant critic sounds like a glamorous lifestyle.','a social critic (= of human society and its organizations ) Social critics have argued that television viewing decreases people''s other social activities.','a critic attacks something Many critics attacked Seurat’s paintings for their lack of colour.','a critic praises something The play was highly praised by critics and the public.','a critic hails something/somebody as something (= describes someone or something as very good ) Critics hailed the film as a brilliant portrayal of American society at that time.','a critic pans something ( also a critic slates something British English ) (= criticizes something strongly ) The television series has been panned by critics.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Critics of the scheme have said that it will not solve the problem of teenage crime.","translation":"منتقدان این طرح گفته اند که این طرح مشکل جرایم نوجوانان را حل نخواهد کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000846858.mp3"},{"sentence":"an outspoken critic of the government","translation":"منتقد صریح دولت","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756115.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('e3521ef8-775d-57f2-85e9-de19528ab428','a2ed1598-c130-5e86-956c-e0697fdd7582',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'armchair critic','نقدگرا، منتقد؛ منتقدان (هنر/سینما)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a film/art/music etc critic He became the chief music critic for the Herald Tribune.','a literary critic (= of books and other literature )','a theatre critic British English , a theater critic American English (= of plays )','a restaurant critic (= of the food, service etc in restaurants ) Being a restaurant critic sounds like a glamorous lifestyle.','a social critic (= of human society and its organizations ) Social critics have argued that television viewing decreases people''s other social activities.','a critic attacks something Many critics attacked Seurat’s paintings for their lack of colour.','a critic praises something The play was highly praised by critics and the public.','a critic hails something/somebody as something (= describes someone or something as very good ) Critics hailed the film as a brilliant portrayal of American society at that time.','a critic pans something ( also a critic slates something British English ) (= criticizes something strongly ) The television series has been panned by critics.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('ab5db6f4-16fd-5950-81fa-b065e7e1e0d2','f8531dc6-eea1-56a2-89bf-9f06e169311d',1,null,null,'spoken & written','something that is done by people in a particular society because it is traditional','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'عادت، رسم؛ گمرگ، حقوق ورودی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a local custom We were unfamiliar with the local customs.','an old/ancient/age-old custom Here on the island, many of the old customs have survived.','an established custom He had criticized some of the school’s established customs.','a traditional custom The children learn about traditional customs, crafts, music, and dance.','a social custom Our people do not want to imitate western social customs.','a French/Greek etc custom The Spanish custom is to add the mother’s surname after the father’s.','a tribal custom He spoke four African languages and knew most of the tribal customs.','burial customs (= things done when someone dies and is buried ) the diversity of burial customs in different parts of the world','follow/observe a custom (= do something that is part of a custom ) Following a Chinese custom, Deng changed his given name to mark the occasion.','respect a custom Strangers should respect the customs of the country they are in.','a custom survives (= continues to be followed ) The custom of slaughtering an animal to welcome guests still survives in some areas.','a custom dies out/disappears (= gradually stops being done ) Sometimes the streets are decorated with flower petals, although this custom is dying out.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The guide offers information on local customs.","translation":"راهنما اطلاعاتی در مورد آداب و رسوم محلی ارائه می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001123056.mp3"},{"sentence":"It’s the custom for the bride’s father to pay for the wedding.","translation":"رسم بر این است که پدر عروس هزینه عروسی را پرداخت می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001123059.mp3"},{"sentence":"The custom of naming women after flowers is becoming less common.","translation":"رسم نامگذاری زنان به نام گل کمتر رایج شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001123062.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('b97967e3-5acc-56e6-8892-5af861b92230','f8531dc6-eea1-56a2-89bf-9f06e169311d',2,null,null,'formal','something that you usually do every day, or in a particular situation','[ singular ]',null,'کاری که معمولا هر روز یا در یک موقعیت خاص انجام می دهید',array['habit']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a local custom We were unfamiliar with the local customs.','an old/ancient/age-old custom Here on the island, many of the old customs have survived.','an established custom He had criticized some of the school’s established customs.','a traditional custom The children learn about traditional customs, crafts, music, and dance.','a social custom Our people do not want to imitate western social customs.','a French/Greek etc custom The Spanish custom is to add the mother’s surname after the father’s.','a tribal custom He spoke four African languages and knew most of the tribal customs.','burial customs (= things done when someone dies and is buried ) the diversity of burial customs in different parts of the world','follow/observe a custom (= do something that is part of a custom ) Following a Chinese custom, Deng changed his given name to mark the occasion.','respect a custom Strangers should respect the customs of the country they are in.','a custom survives (= continues to be followed ) The custom of slaughtering an animal to welcome guests still survives in some areas.','a custom dies out/disappears (= gradually stops being done ) Sometimes the streets are decorated with flower petals, although this custom is dying out.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"He awoke early, as was his custom.","translation":"طبق عادتش زود از خواب بیدار شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001123072.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
