('2a25dcfe-ef17-5f17-8739-e18ce715e7b7','b39da7b9-daa7-543c-bc1b-b91cb885d021',1,null,null,'spoken & written','discussion of a particular subject that often continues for a long time and in which people express different opinions','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'مناظره، بحث؛ مباحثه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['considerable debate There has been considerable debate about the way forward for education.','lively debate (= interesting and involving a lot of different opinions ) The conference produced some lively debate.','intense debate (= in which people put forward strong and different arguments ) The future of the nuclear industry has been a matter of intense debate.','a heated/fierce debate (= in which people express strong opinions in an angry way ) There has been a fierce debate over the way the war was fought.','a wider debate (= involving more people or a more general discussion ) We believe that there should be a wider debate on such an important issue.','a public debate (= in which people put forward their ideas publicly, so that everyone can form an opinion. ) He called for a public debate on race and discrimination.','national debate (= one that involves everyone in a country ) It is time to start a national debate on the future of the health service.','political debate (= involving members of political parties ) There was much political debate on pensions reform.','long-running debate (= continuing for a long time ) the long-running debate about the future of our inner cities','ongoing debate (= still continuing ) This is unlikely to be the final word in this ongoing debate.','have a debate I think we should have a public debate on this issue.','provoke/spark/trigger debate (= cause a debate to start ) The episode provoked fierce debate about freedom of speech.','stifle debate (= prevent people from having a debate ) How can the party stifle debate on such an important issue?','debate rages (= happens over a period of time and and involves strong feelings ) A national debate is now raging over the level of youth crime.','be the subject of debate (= be something that people discuss ) Teaching methods have long been the subject of debate.','be a matter of debate (= be something that people have discussed ) The effectiveness of the government’s policy has been a matter of fierce debate.','be a matter for debate (= be something that people should discuss ) The future of the police force is a matter for public debate.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the gun-control debate in the US","translation":"بحث کنترل اسلحه در آمریکا","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001684745.mp3"},{"sentence":"The new drug has become the subject of heated debate within the medical profession.","translation":"داروی جدید به موضوع بحث های داغ در حرفه پزشکی تبدیل شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001684751.mp3"},{"sentence":"There has been widespread public debate over the introduction of genetically modified food.","translation":"بحث عمومی گسترده ای در مورد معرفی مواد غذایی اصلاح شده ژنتیکی وجود داشته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001962179.mp3"},{"sentence":"There was much lively debate about whether women should spend more time in the home.","translation":"بحث های پر جنب و جوش زیادی در مورد اینکه آیا زنان باید زمان بیشتری را در خانه بگذرانند وجود داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001962183.mp3"},{"sentence":"A fierce debate raged over which artist’s work should be chosen for the prize.","translation":"بحث شدیدی در مورد اینکه کدام اثر هنرمند باید برای جایزه انتخاب شود، درگرفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001962187.mp3"},{"sentence":"the ongoing debate between environmentalists and the road-building lobby over the future of our countryside","translation":"مناظره جاری بین محیط بانان و لابی راه سازی بر سر آینده روستای ما","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001962193.mp3"},{"sentence":"Nuclear power has always been a topic that has sparked off considerable debate .","translation":"انرژی هسته ای همیشه موضوعی بوده است که بحث های قابل توجهی را برانگیخته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001962197.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
('4d053b04-961f-5834-acb4-2b5caafd7461','b39da7b9-daa7-543c-bc1b-b91cb885d021',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a formal discussion of a particular problem, subject etc in which people express different opinions, and sometimes vote on them','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'یک بحث رسمی در مورد یک مشکل خاص، موضوع و غیره که در آن افراد نظرات متفاوتی را بیان می کنند و گاهی اوقات به آنها رأی می دهند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['considerable debate There has been considerable debate about the way forward for education.','lively debate (= interesting and involving a lot of different opinions ) The conference produced some lively debate.','intense debate (= in which people put forward strong and different arguments ) The future of the nuclear industry has been a matter of intense debate.','a heated/fierce debate (= in which people express strong opinions in an angry way ) There has been a fierce debate over the way the war was fought.','a wider debate (= involving more people or a more general discussion ) We believe that there should be a wider debate on such an important issue.','a public debate (= in which people put forward their ideas publicly, so that everyone can form an opinion. ) He called for a public debate on race and discrimination.','national debate (= one that involves everyone in a country ) It is time to start a national debate on the future of the health service.','political debate (= involving members of political parties ) There was much political debate on pensions reform.','long-running debate (= continuing for a long time ) the long-running debate about the future of our inner cities','ongoing debate (= still continuing ) This is unlikely to be the final word in this ongoing debate.','have a debate I think we should have a public debate on this issue.','provoke/spark/trigger debate (= cause a debate to start ) The episode provoked fierce debate about freedom of speech.','stifle debate (= prevent people from having a debate ) How can the party stifle debate on such an important issue?','debate rages (= happens over a period of time and and involves strong feelings ) A national debate is now raging over the level of youth crime.','be the subject of debate (= be something that people discuss ) Teaching methods have long been the subject of debate.','be a matter of debate (= be something that people have discussed ) The effectiveness of the government’s policy has been a matter of fierce debate.','be a matter for debate (= be something that people should discuss ) The future of the police force is a matter for public debate.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a debate on legalized gambling","translation":"بحث در مورد قمار قانونی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001684752.mp3"},{"sentence":"a televised debate","translation":"یک مناظره تلویزیونی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000439.mp3"},{"sentence":"It would have been better to hold the debate during the day.","translation":"بهتر بود مناظره در روز برگزار می شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001684756.mp3"},{"sentence":"What topics are under debate in Congress this week?","translation":"چه موضوعاتی در این هفته در کنگره مورد بحث است؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001684759.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('7ae86d9e-dfa2-5b94-b935-be57473150e7','b39da7b9-daa7-543c-bc1b-b91cb885d021',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be open to debate','مناظره، بحث؛ مباحثه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['considerable debate There has been considerable debate about the way forward for education.','lively debate (= interesting and involving a lot of different opinions ) The conference produced some lively debate.','intense debate (= in which people put forward strong and different arguments ) The future of the nuclear industry has been a matter of intense debate.','a heated/fierce debate (= in which people express strong opinions in an angry way ) There has been a fierce debate over the way the war was fought.','a wider debate (= involving more people or a more general discussion ) We believe that there should be a wider debate on such an important issue.','a public debate (= in which people put forward their ideas publicly, so that everyone can form an opinion. ) He called for a public debate on race and discrimination.','national debate (= one that involves everyone in a country ) It is time to start a national debate on the future of the health service.','political debate (= involving members of political parties ) There was much political debate on pensions reform.','long-running debate (= continuing for a long time ) the long-running debate about the future of our inner cities','ongoing debate (= still continuing ) This is unlikely to be the final word in this ongoing debate.','have a debate I think we should have a public debate on this issue.','provoke/spark/trigger debate (= cause a debate to start ) The episode provoked fierce debate about freedom of speech.','stifle debate (= prevent people from having a debate ) How can the party stifle debate on such an important issue?','debate rages (= happens over a period of time and and involves strong feelings ) A national debate is now raging over the level of youth crime.','be the subject of debate (= be something that people discuss ) Teaching methods have long been the subject of debate.','be a matter of debate (= be something that people have discussed ) The effectiveness of the government’s policy has been a matter of fierce debate.','be a matter for debate (= be something that people should discuss ) The future of the police force is a matter for public debate.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('72f2a866-a404-5163-a574-095cb1dcee79','abe81f54-0fc5-5bbe-b7f6-0b291025aeee',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to discuss a subject formally when you are trying to make a decision or find a solution',null,null,'زمانی که در تلاش برای تصمیم گیری یا یافتن راه حل هستید، درباره موضوعی به طور رسمی بحث کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The issue will be debated on Tuesday.","translation":"این موضوع روز سه شنبه مورد بحث قرار خواهد گرفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001684761.mp3"},{"sentence":"Meanwhile, philosophers debate whether it’s right to clone an individual.","translation":"در همین حال، فیلسوفان بحث می کنند که آیا شبیه سازی یک فرد درست است یا خیر.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000834770.mp3"},{"sentence":"an invitation to debate with William on the future of democracy","translation":"دعوت به مناظره با ویلیام در مورد آینده دموکراسی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000440.mp3"},{"sentence":"His conclusions are hotly debated (= argued about strongly ) .","translation":"نتیجه گیری های او به شدت مورد بحث است (= به شدت درباره آن بحث می شود).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000834774.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('4582cc3c-8701-5795-a1a6-37fa5815f320','abe81f54-0fc5-5bbe-b7f6-0b291025aeee',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to consider something carefully before making a decision',null,null,'قبل از تصمیم گیری، چیزی را به دقت در نظر بگیرید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I debated with myself whether I should tell anyone.","translation":"با خودم بحث کردم که آیا به کسی بگویم یا نه.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000834780.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’m still debating what to do.","translation":"من هنوز در حال بحث هستم که چه کار کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000834783.mp3"},{"sentence":"For a moment Mary debated telling Rick the truth.","translation":"برای لحظه ای مری در مورد گفتن حقیقت به ریک بحث کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000441.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('5d01b275-5c88-5671-b281-875cc7c37fa8','2d605fc1-a3c6-59d8-8d9e-c5001f899c58',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a period of 10 years',null,null,'دهه، دوره ده‌ساله','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('2e11aa16-fa43-51da-ac36-006e21a00059','33a488a8-3aac-543a-9003-c0bde15a38a6',1,null,null,'spoken & written','of a good enough standard or quality','[ usually before noun ]',null,'پسندیده، درست و دربست؛ (آدم) نرم‌خو','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a decent salary","translation":"حقوق مناسب","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-002084282.mp3"},{"sentence":"Don’t you have a decent jacket?","translation":"آیا یک ژاکت مناسب ندارید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001685267.mp3"},{"sentence":"a house with a decent-sized yard","translation":"خانه ای با حیاط مناسب","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001131487.mp3"},{"sentence":"Their in-flight magazine is halfway decent (= quite good ) .","translation":"مجله حین پرواز آنها در نیمه راه مناسب است (= کاملاً خوب).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001685271.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('342ba595-94af-5309-9484-90c2e085226a','33a488a8-3aac-543a-9003-c0bde15a38a6',2,null,null,'spoken & written','following moral standards that are acceptable to society',null,null,'پیروی از معیارهای اخلاقی قابل قبول برای جامعه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The majority of residents here are decent citizens.","translation":"اکثر ساکنان اینجا شهروندان شایسته هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001685283.mp3"},{"sentence":"a decent burial","translation":"دفن شایسته","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001685284.mp3"},{"sentence":"Paul visited the local bars more frequently than was decent for a senior lecturer.","translation":"پل بیشتر از آنچه برای یک مدرس ارشد مناسب بود، بارهای محلی را بازدید می کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001685285.mp3"},{"sentence":"The chairman did the decent thing (= did what people thought he ought to ) and resigned.","translation":"رئیس کار شایسته ای را انجام داد (= کاری که مردم فکر می کردند باید انجام دهد) و استعفا داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001685286.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('aca804a6-fd33-5a58-9c50-86d0e28b4ccc','33a488a8-3aac-543a-9003-c0bde15a38a6',3,null,null,'spoken & written','treating people in a fair and kind way','[ usually before noun ]',null,'رفتار منصفانه و مهربانانه با مردم','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I decided her father was a decent guy after all.","translation":"من تصمیم گرفتم که پدرش پسر خوبی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001131491.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was decent of you to show up today.","translation":"خیلی خوب بود که امروز حاضر شدی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001131494.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('2c91093c-f836-542e-806a-32dfca7ce8d7','33a488a8-3aac-543a-9003-c0bde15a38a6',4,null,null,'spoken & written','wearing enough clothes so that you do not show too much of your body – used humorously',null,null,'به اندازه کافی لباس بپوشید تا بیش از حد بدن خود را نشان ندهید - به صورت طنز استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Are you decent? Can I come in?","translation":"آیا شما شایسته هستید؟ میتونم بیام داخل؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001131512.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('7d2cf0ae-6094-5d2c-b982-514fb0b72383','1fc3b8c0-2d5c-564a-9227-4c8335429da8',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to make a choice or judgment about something, especially after considering all the possibilities or arguments','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'تصمیم گرفتن؛ تصمیم، اظهار (درباره)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Has anything been decided yet?","translation":"آیا هنوز چیزی قطعی شده است؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001684950.mp3"},{"sentence":"Tina’s decided to go to Rome for her holidays.","translation":"تینا تصمیم گرفت برای تعطیلاتش به رم برود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000835521.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was decided that four hospitals should close.","translation":"قرار شد چهار بیمارستان تعطیل شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000835524.mp3"},{"sentence":"I can’t decide whether I like him or not.","translation":"نمی توانم تصمیم بگیرم که او را دوست دارم یا نه.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000835527.mp3"},{"sentence":"People have a right to decide how to spend their own money.","translation":"مردم حق دارند تصمیم بگیرند که چگونه پول خود را خرج کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001684957.mp3"},{"sentence":"A meeting was called to decide between the three candidates.","translation":"جلسه ای برای تصمیم گیری بین سه نامزد تشکیل شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000835533.mp3"},{"sentence":"You must decide for yourself.","translation":"خودت باید تصمیم بگیری","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000835540.mp3"},{"sentence":"The trainees decide among themselves what programs to take.","translation":"کارآموزان بین خودشان تصمیم می گیرند که چه برنامه هایی را اجرا کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001684963.mp3"},{"sentence":"He eventually decided against telling her.","translation":"او در نهایت تصمیم گرفت که به او چیزی نگوید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001684958.mp3"},{"sentence":"After a long discussion, they decided in favour of (= chose ) the older applicant.","translation":"پس از یک بحث طولانی، آنها به نفع (= انتخاب) متقاضی مسن تر تصمیم گرفتند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001684967.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was decided that he should resign.","translation":"تصمیم گرفته شد که استعفا دهد.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,11),
('d90e3c0a-98a5-53d3-bd98-97f6d0e8d943','1fc3b8c0-2d5c-564a-9227-4c8335429da8',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to influence a situation or event so that a particular result is produced','[ transitive ]',null,'تأثیر گذاشتن بر یک موقعیت یا رویداد به طوری که نتیجه خاصی حاصل شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"It was the penalty kick that decided the match.","translation":"این ضربه پنالتی بود که بازی را رقم زد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001684972.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('e47e42c1-c7cb-519d-aeab-f1e1ae2eb66c','1fc3b8c0-2d5c-564a-9227-4c8335429da8',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to be the reason for someone making a particular choice','[ transitive ]',null,'دلیلی برای انتخاب خاص کسی باشد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Taxes could be the deciding factor for millions of floating voters.","translation":"مالیات ها می تواند عامل تعیین کننده برای میلیون ها رای دهنده شناور باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000835556.mp3"},{"sentence":"The look he gave her decided her not to ask.","translation":"نگاهی که به او کرد تصمیم گرفت که او نپرسد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000835552.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('14e6cb06-6545-5f84-a11e-83558c5a763a','1fc3b8c0-2d5c-564a-9227-4c8335429da8',4,null,null,'law','to make an official or legal judgment','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'برای صدور حکم رسمی یا قانونی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The Commission will have the power to decide disputes.","translation":"کمیسیون قدرت تصمیم گیری در مورد اختلافات را خواهد داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001684980.mp3"},{"sentence":"If the Parole Board decides in his favour, the prisoner will be released.","translation":"اگر هیئت آزادی مشروط به نفع او تصمیم بگیرد، زندانی آزاد خواهد شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000835579.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('fb626616-7585-5a4e-8888-a0cfb141bc2d','8174da6b-e2aa-5c81-9d5f-6c2feecd5a03',1,null,null,'spoken & written','used to emphasize that a belief , feeling, opinion etc is very strong, important, or sincere',null,null,'عمیقاً، به‌نحو ژرف؛ به‌شدت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Her lies hurt my father deeply.","translation":"دروغ های او پدرم را عمیقا آزار می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000837665.mp3"},{"sentence":"She is deeply upset.","translation":"او به شدت ناراحت است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001706476.mp3"},{"sentence":"He loves her deeply.","translation":"او را عمیقا دوست دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001706477.mp3"},{"sentence":"Teachers are deeply divided on this issue.","translation":"معلمان در این موضوع عمیقاً اختلاف نظر دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001706478.mp3"},{"sentence":"deeply held religious beliefs","translation":"اعتقادات مذهبی عمیق","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001706479.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('0d8b8c86-1285-5b9c-beca-1c930c38bf7b','8174da6b-e2aa-5c81-9d5f-6c2feecd5a03',2,null,null,'spoken & written','in a serious , careful way',null,null,'به روشی جدی و دقیق','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Most doctors think deeply about what their patients want.","translation":"اکثر پزشکان عمیقاً به آنچه بیمارانشان می خواهند فکر می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001706483.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
