('2c95eb0d-1def-5626-aaeb-57fa57e860a6','dfab53d3-4b93-5b3e-83ec-eeb9c860593c',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to notice or discover something, especially something that is not easy to see, hear etc',null,null,'کشف کردن، دریافتن (چیز پنهان)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Many forms of cancer can be cured if detected early.","translation":"بسیاری از انواع سرطان در صورت تشخیص زودهنگام قابل درمان هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000820695.mp3"},{"sentence":"Dan detected a change in her mood.","translation":"دن متوجه تغییر در خلق و خوی او شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001716271.mp3"},{"sentence":"Do I detect a note of sarcasm in your voice?","translation":"آیا در صدای شما یک نت طعنه تشخیص می دهم؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000820696.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('d309b82b-cf98-5961-b19b-3d4a6cd343e7','19842aba-6d1e-5073-989a-b76dd20f5c0e',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a machine or tool that does a special job',null,null,'دستگاه، ابزار؛ ترفند',array['gadget']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['an electronic device The shops are always full of new electronic devices.','a mechanical device (= using power from an engine or machine ) One day it will be technically possible to replace patients’ hearts with mechanical devices.','a simple device He invented a simple device for chopping onions.','a clever device (= made using a clever idea ) This clever little device rings to tell you where you left your keys.','a labour-saving device British English , a labor-saving device American English (= that reduces the amount of work you have to do ) Modern houses have so many labour-saving devices.','a security device (= designed to protect against crime ) Cars today have better alarms and security devices.','a safety device (= designed to keep people safe ) The accident happened because a simple safety device wasn’t properly fitted.','a handheld device (= that you hold in your hand ) This is a handheld device for playing electronic games.','a storage device (= a computer device for storing information electronically ) You may need an additional storage device if you have a lot of data.','a medical device The company makes medical devices that use laser technology for correcting eye disorders.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"modern labour-saving devices","translation":"دستگاه های مدرن صرفه جویی در کار","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001140862.mp3"},{"sentence":"a device for separating metal from garbage","translation":"وسیله ای برای جدا کردن فلز از زباله","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001140861.mp3"},{"sentence":"The company makes devices to detect carbon monoxide.","translation":"این شرکت دستگاه هایی برای تشخیص مونوکسید کربن می سازد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001743686.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('72fb3d94-b190-5c7c-9fab-f1aee680ca00','19842aba-6d1e-5073-989a-b76dd20f5c0e',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a special way of doing something that makes it easier to do',null,null,'یک روش خاص برای انجام کاری که انجام آن را آسان تر می کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['an electronic device The shops are always full of new electronic devices.','a mechanical device (= using power from an engine or machine ) One day it will be technically possible to replace patients’ hearts with mechanical devices.','a simple device He invented a simple device for chopping onions.','a clever device (= made using a clever idea ) This clever little device rings to tell you where you left your keys.','a labour-saving device British English , a labor-saving device American English (= that reduces the amount of work you have to do ) Modern houses have so many labour-saving devices.','a security device (= designed to protect against crime ) Cars today have better alarms and security devices.','a safety device (= designed to keep people safe ) The accident happened because a simple safety device wasn’t properly fitted.','a handheld device (= that you hold in your hand ) This is a handheld device for playing electronic games.','a storage device (= a computer device for storing information electronically ) You may need an additional storage device if you have a lot of data.','a medical device The company makes medical devices that use laser technology for correcting eye disorders.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Testing yourself with information on cards is a useful device for studying.","translation":"تست کردن خود با اطلاعات روی کارت ها وسیله ای مفید برای مطالعه است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001140885.mp3"},{"sentence":"a memory device","translation":"یک دستگاه حافظه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001743689.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('96efe9b1-0262-5bab-8dc8-06ce6ae7b55e','19842aba-6d1e-5073-989a-b76dd20f5c0e',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a plan or trick , especially for a dishonest purpose',null,null,'یک نقشه یا ترفند، به ویژه برای یک هدف غیر صادقانه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['an electronic device The shops are always full of new electronic devices.','a mechanical device (= using power from an engine or machine ) One day it will be technically possible to replace patients’ hearts with mechanical devices.','a simple device He invented a simple device for chopping onions.','a clever device (= made using a clever idea ) This clever little device rings to tell you where you left your keys.','a labour-saving device British English , a labor-saving device American English (= that reduces the amount of work you have to do ) Modern houses have so many labour-saving devices.','a security device (= designed to protect against crime ) Cars today have better alarms and security devices.','a safety device (= designed to keep people safe ) The accident happened because a simple safety device wasn’t properly fitted.','a handheld device (= that you hold in your hand ) This is a handheld device for playing electronic games.','a storage device (= a computer device for storing information electronically ) You may need an additional storage device if you have a lot of data.','a medical device The company makes medical devices that use laser technology for correcting eye disorders.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Their proposal was only a device to confuse the opposition.","translation":"پیشنهاد آنها تنها ابزاری برای سردرگمی مخالفان بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001140879.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('7bcdb238-a3c4-51ce-b891-00098eb9fdbe','19842aba-6d1e-5073-989a-b76dd20f5c0e',4,null,null,'spoken & written','a bomb or other explosive weapon',null,null,'یک بمب یا سلاح انفجاری دیگر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['an electronic device The shops are always full of new electronic devices.','a mechanical device (= using power from an engine or machine ) One day it will be technically possible to replace patients’ hearts with mechanical devices.','a simple device He invented a simple device for chopping onions.','a clever device (= made using a clever idea ) This clever little device rings to tell you where you left your keys.','a labour-saving device British English , a labor-saving device American English (= that reduces the amount of work you have to do ) Modern houses have so many labour-saving devices.','a security device (= designed to protect against crime ) Cars today have better alarms and security devices.','a safety device (= designed to keep people safe ) The accident happened because a simple safety device wasn’t properly fitted.','a handheld device (= that you hold in your hand ) This is a handheld device for playing electronic games.','a storage device (= a computer device for storing information electronically ) You may need an additional storage device if you have a lot of data.','a medical device The company makes medical devices that use laser technology for correcting eye disorders.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('7cb7d442-c8e1-51ea-accd-e1b680000f78','19842aba-6d1e-5073-989a-b76dd20f5c0e',5,null,null,'spoken & written','the special use of words in literature , or of words, lights etc in a play, to achieve an effect',null,null,'استفاده ویژه از کلمات در ادبیات، یا از کلمات، نورها و غیره در نمایشنامه برای رسیدن به اثر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['an electronic device The shops are always full of new electronic devices.','a mechanical device (= using power from an engine or machine ) One day it will be technically possible to replace patients’ hearts with mechanical devices.','a simple device He invented a simple device for chopping onions.','a clever device (= made using a clever idea ) This clever little device rings to tell you where you left your keys.','a labour-saving device British English , a labor-saving device American English (= that reduces the amount of work you have to do ) Modern houses have so many labour-saving devices.','a security device (= designed to protect against crime ) Cars today have better alarms and security devices.','a safety device (= designed to keep people safe ) The accident happened because a simple safety device wasn’t properly fitted.','a handheld device (= that you hold in your hand ) This is a handheld device for playing electronic games.','a storage device (= a computer device for storing information electronically ) You may need an additional storage device if you have a lot of data.','a medical device The company makes medical devices that use laser technology for correcting eye disorders.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Metaphor is a common literary device.","translation":"استعاره یک ابزار ادبی رایج است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001140899.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('88938c2f-4e0d-56e7-917e-e8e94e6a6e08','153d78da-1d5e-59f2-a7b0-b40f1cfa0cd9',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to be different from something in some way',null,null,'متفاوت بودن، فرق کردن؛ ناسازگار بودن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['differ greatly/enormously Modern teaching methods differ greatly from those fifty years ago.','differ significantly (= in an important way ) The second set of test results did not differ significantly from the first.','differ considerably/widely/substantially (= greatly ) Opinions differ widely on the best way to do this.','differ sharply/noticeably/markedly (= in a very noticeable way ) Ways of negotiating differ markedly across the Atlantic.','differ radically (= very greatly ) The new car differed radically from the earlier model.','differ fundamentally (= in a very basic way ) These paintings differed fundamentally from his earlier work.','differ slightly Prices differ slightly from one shop to another.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The two systems differ in many respects.","translation":"این دو سیستم از بسیاری جهات با هم تفاوت دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001690015.mp3"},{"sentence":"People differ from one another in their ability to handle stress.","translation":"افراد در توانایی کنترل استرس با یکدیگر تفاوت دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001142886.mp3"},{"sentence":"The symptoms did not differ between the two groups.","translation":"علائم بین دو گروه تفاوتی نداشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001690018.mp3"},{"sentence":"We soon found that prices differed enormously.","translation":"به زودی متوجه شدیم که قیمت ها بسیار متفاوت است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001142889.mp3"},{"sentence":"Experts have differing views on the subject.","translation":"کارشناسان نظرات متفاوتی در این زمینه دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001690019.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('c5709afb-c541-5004-8ac9-1498629a2de2','153d78da-1d5e-59f2-a7b0-b40f1cfa0cd9',2,null,null,'spoken & written','if two people or groups differ about something, they have opposite opinions',null,null,'اگر دو نفر یا گروه در مورد چیزی اختلاف نظر داشته باشند، نظرات مخالف دارند',array['disagree']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['differ greatly/enormously Modern teaching methods differ greatly from those fifty years ago.','differ significantly (= in an important way ) The second set of test results did not differ significantly from the first.','differ considerably/widely/substantially (= greatly ) Opinions differ widely on the best way to do this.','differ sharply/noticeably/markedly (= in a very noticeable way ) Ways of negotiating differ markedly across the Atlantic.','differ radically (= very greatly ) The new car differed radically from the earlier model.','differ fundamentally (= in a very basic way ) These paintings differed fundamentally from his earlier work.','differ slightly Prices differ slightly from one shop to another.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The two lawyers differed about how to present the case.","translation":"دو وکیل در مورد نحوه ارائه پرونده اختلاف نظر داشتند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001142896.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
