('b84d2733-d4db-5b8f-a463-200f35354430','4fe6a1ee-dfec-5864-add5-cfdf205ac952',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the main meal of the day, eaten in the middle of the day or the evening','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'شام، صرف غذا (اصلی)؛ ضیافت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have/eat dinner Why don''t you come and have dinner with us?','make/cook dinner I offered to cook dinner.','have something for dinner I thought we might have pasta for dinner tonight.','have somebody for/to dinner We''re having a few friends round to dinner.','ask/invite somebody to dinner Let''s ask Kate and Mike to dinner.','come for/to dinner Mark is coming over for dinner.','go out for/to dinner (= go and eat in a restaurant ) Would you like to go out for dinner on Saturday?','serve dinner (= start giving people food ) Dinner is served between 7 and 11 pm in the hotel restaurant.','a three-course/four-course etc dinner The cost of the hotel includes a three-course dinner.','Sunday/Christmas/Thanksgiving dinner (= a special meal eaten on Sunday etc ) We usually have a walk after Christmas dinner.','a romantic dinner (= for two people in a romantic relationship ) Clive and Denise were enjoying a romantic dinner for two in a quiet French restaurant.','a candle-lit dinner (= with only candles for lighting ) Chris treated his girlfriend to a candle-lit dinner.','a leisurely dinner (= not hurried ) I enjoy having a leisurely dinner with some friends at the weekend.','a black-tie dinner (= where people wear special formal clothes ) He was invited to a black-tie dinner at one of the Oxford colleges.','a slap-up dinner British English informal (= with a lot of good food ) Mum always makes a slap-up dinner for me when I go home.','school dinners British English (= meals provided at school in the middle of the day ) School dinners are served in the canteen.','TV dinners (= meals that you eat while watching TV ) TV dinners in aluminium containers can be found in the freezer departments of many supermarkets.','a dinner party (= when someone''s friends are invited for a special evening meal ) We are having a dinner party on Saturday.','a dinner guest The dinner guests began arriving at about seven o''clock.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"What time do you usually have dinner?","translation":"معمولا چه ساعتی شام می خورید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000459.mp3"},{"sentence":"We’re having fish for dinner tonight.","translation":"ما امشب برای شام ماهی می خوریم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000460.mp3"},{"sentence":"What''s for dinner?","translation":"شام چی؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000461.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('fb6f7802-9289-56c3-8ffc-d963c33a4463','4fe6a1ee-dfec-5864-add5-cfdf205ac952',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a formal occasion when an evening meal is eaten, often to celebrate something','[ countable ]',null,'یک مناسبت رسمی هنگام صرف یک وعده عصرانه، اغلب برای جشن گرفتن چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have/eat dinner Why don''t you come and have dinner with us?','make/cook dinner I offered to cook dinner.','have something for dinner I thought we might have pasta for dinner tonight.','have somebody for/to dinner We''re having a few friends round to dinner.','ask/invite somebody to dinner Let''s ask Kate and Mike to dinner.','come for/to dinner Mark is coming over for dinner.','go out for/to dinner (= go and eat in a restaurant ) Would you like to go out for dinner on Saturday?','serve dinner (= start giving people food ) Dinner is served between 7 and 11 pm in the hotel restaurant.','a three-course/four-course etc dinner The cost of the hotel includes a three-course dinner.','Sunday/Christmas/Thanksgiving dinner (= a special meal eaten on Sunday etc ) We usually have a walk after Christmas dinner.','a romantic dinner (= for two people in a romantic relationship ) Clive and Denise were enjoying a romantic dinner for two in a quiet French restaurant.','a candle-lit dinner (= with only candles for lighting ) Chris treated his girlfriend to a candle-lit dinner.','a leisurely dinner (= not hurried ) I enjoy having a leisurely dinner with some friends at the weekend.','a black-tie dinner (= where people wear special formal clothes ) He was invited to a black-tie dinner at one of the Oxford colleges.','a slap-up dinner British English informal (= with a lot of good food ) Mum always makes a slap-up dinner for me when I go home.','school dinners British English (= meals provided at school in the middle of the day ) School dinners are served in the canteen.','TV dinners (= meals that you eat while watching TV ) TV dinners in aluminium containers can be found in the freezer departments of many supermarkets.','a dinner party (= when someone''s friends are invited for a special evening meal ) We are having a dinner party on Saturday.','a dinner guest The dinner guests began arriving at about seven o''clock.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the Club’s annual dinner","translation":"شام سالانه باشگاه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001144557.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('c04c08d2-34d8-5f9f-8566-74355f8b37d1','788b0336-794e-5508-86a6-84cf79f54230',1,'without involving others','بدون دخالت دیگران','spoken & written','done without any other people, actions, processes etc coming between',null,null,'مستقیم، بی‌واسطه؛ بی‌پرده؛ روبه‌رو','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['direct access Very few people have direct access to the president.','direct contact The disease is only spread by direct contact between people.','a direct link/connection The campaign makes a direct link between global warming and the consumption of energy in the home.','a direct relationship We think having a direct relationship with customers is very important.','a direct effect/impact Our organization’s work has a direct impact upon children’s lives in this country.','a direct result/consequence Many illnesses here are a direct consequence of bad diet.','direct experience People learn best through direct experience.','direct evidence There is no direct evidence that this causes any harm.','direct control The state has direct control over certain industries.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Experienced users have direct access to the main data files.","translation":"کاربران با تجربه به فایل های داده اصلی دسترسی مستقیم دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001144782.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’m not in direct contact with them.","translation":"من با آنها ارتباط مستقیم ندارم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001144784.mp3"},{"sentence":"Few policy-makers have had direct experience of business.","translation":"تعداد کمی از سیاستگذاران تجربه مستقیم از تجارت داشته اند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001144783.mp3"},{"sentence":"Educational level has a sizeable direct effect on income.","translation":"سطح تحصیلات تأثیر مستقیم قابل توجهی بر درآمد دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001694856.mp3"},{"sentence":"There is a direct link between poverty and ill-health.","translation":"ارتباط مستقیمی بین فقر و بیماری وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001694859.mp3"},{"sentence":"The decision to close the hospital is a direct result of Government health policy.","translation":"تصمیم برای تعطیلی بیمارستان نتیجه مستقیم سیاست های بهداشتی دولت است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001694862.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
