('453994f1-d2cb-533c-a3f4-c1e5e332ee3b','f064b920-5339-563f-ae5b-79674cf725a1',6,null,null,'spoken & written','a note written by your doctor or one of your parents saying that you were ill on a particular day',null,null,'یادداشتی که توسط پزشک یا یکی از والدینتان نوشته شده است که می گوید شما در یک روز خاص بیمار بودید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('2182cd5d-cc01-574b-b92e-006d56e60a7c','a40ce021-456d-55c0-a33c-d4b1f881afe1',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to become larger in size , number, or amount, or to make something become larger','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'گسترش یافتن، بزرگ شدن؛ شرح دادن (موضوع)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Water expands as it freezes.","translation":"آب با یخ زدن منبسط می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001230937.mp3"},{"sentence":"Sydney’s population expanded rapidly in the 1960s.","translation":"جمعیت سیدنی در دهه 1960 به سرعت افزایش یافت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001230938.mp3"},{"sentence":"exercises that expand the chest muscles","translation":"ورزش هایی که عضلات سینه را گسترش می دهند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001230941.mp3"},{"sentence":"his expanding waistline","translation":"دور کمر در حال گسترش او","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001612021.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('0cdc72d1-66b5-5879-924d-8f554e1992fc','a40ce021-456d-55c0-a33c-d4b1f881afe1',2,null,null,'spoken & written','if a company, business etc expands, or if someone expands it, they open new shops , factories etc','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'اگر یک شرکت، تجارت و غیره گسترش یابد، یا اگر کسی آن را گسترش دهد، مغازه‌ها، کارخانه‌ها و غیره جدیدی باز می‌کنند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The computer industry has expanded greatly over the last decade.","translation":"صنعت کامپیوتر در دهه گذشته بسیار گسترش یافته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001612022.mp3"},{"sentence":"The hotel wants to expand its business by adding a swimming pool.","translation":"این هتل می خواهد تجارت خود را با اضافه کردن یک استخر گسترش دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001612023.mp3"},{"sentence":"the rapidly expanding field of information technology","translation":"حوزه فناوری اطلاعات که به سرعت در حال گسترش است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001612024.mp3"},{"sentence":"We have plans to expand into the U.S. market.","translation":"ما برنامه هایی برای گسترش به بازار ایالات متحده داریم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001612030.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('f3fd3f12-b2ad-5245-979e-2f8a235cd45d','a40ce021-456d-55c0-a33c-d4b1f881afe1',3,null,null,'literary','to become more confident and start to talk more','[ intransitive ]',null,'اعتماد به نفس بیشتری پیدا کنید و شروع به صحبت کردن کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"After a few whiskies he started to expand a little.","translation":"بعد از چند ویسکی شروع به گسترش کمی کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001230961.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('e59031d0-9a87-5eee-8804-907de969d93a','10b9d129-1b64-5b2f-b399-a5aee9054723',1,'think something will happen','فکر کن اتفاقی خواهد افتاد','spoken & written','to think that something will happen because it seems likely or has been planned',null,null,'انتظار داشتن، چشم‌داشتن؛ مأمور (کار)؛ باردار بودن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['fully expect (= completely ) We fully expected to win.','confidently expect (= with a feeling of confidence ) He confidently expected to be elected again.','half expect (= partly, but not completely ) He walked slowly towards the box, half expecting it to explode.','really expect (= definitely ) I didn’t really expect her to come.','honestly expect (= really expect ) Do you honestly expect me to look after the kids while you go on holiday?','hardly expect (= almost not ) You can hardly expect a child of three to know the difference between right and wrong.','rightly expect (= with good reason ) The public rightly expects government officials to be honest.','as expected (= in the way that was planned or thought likely to happen ) Tickets have not been selling as well as expected.','something is (only) to be expected (= used to say that you are not surprised by something unpleasant ) After all this rain, some flooding is only to be expected.','something happens when you least expect it Bad luck tends to happen when you least expect it.','somebody is entitled to expect something (= have the right to think something will happen ) You’re entitled to expect decent service at these prices.','it is reasonable/unreasonable to expect something It’s unreasonable to expect a tenant to pay for repairs to the outside of the house.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I expect to be back within a week.","translation":"من انتظار دارم تا یک هفته دیگر برگردم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653652.mp3"},{"sentence":"The company expects to complete work in April.","translation":"این شرکت انتظار دارد کار را در ماه آوریل به پایان برساند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653653.mp3"},{"sentence":"Emergency repairs were expected to take three weeks.","translation":"انتظار می رفت تعمیرات اضطراری سه هفته طول بکشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001231988.mp3"},{"sentence":"I didn’t expect him to stay so long.","translation":"انتظار نداشتم اینقدر طولانی بماند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653656.mp3"},{"sentence":"There’s the doorbell – I expect it’ll be my mother.","translation":"زنگ در است - من انتظار دارم که مادر من باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001231985.mp3"},{"sentence":"He will be hard to beat. I fully expect (= am completely sure about ) that and I’m ready.","translation":"شکست دادن او سخت خواهد بود. من کاملاً انتظار دارم (= کاملاً در مورد آن مطمئن هستم) و من آماده هستم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653659.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘Who are you?’ he murmured, only half expecting (= thinking it was possible, but not likely ) her to answer.","translation":"او زمزمه کرد: «تو کی هستی؟»، فقط نیمی از انتظار (= فکر می‌کرد که ممکن است، اما به احتمال زیاد) پاسخ دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653664.mp3"},{"sentence":"He didn’t get his expected pay rise.","translation":"او افزایش دستمزد مورد انتظار خود را دریافت نکرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653669.mp3"},{"sentence":"As expected, the whole family was shocked by the news.","translation":"همانطور که انتظار می رفت، تمام خانواده از این خبر شوکه شدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001232003.mp3"},{"sentence":"A little nervousness is only to be expected when you are starting a new job.","translation":"فقط زمانی که در حال شروع یک کار جدید هستید، کمی عصبی بودن قابل انتظار است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001232007.mp3"}]'::jsonb,10),
('3d35c100-31ee-5a77-865c-7651be86ebb2','10b9d129-1b64-5b2f-b399-a5aee9054723',2,'demand','تقاضا','spoken & written','to demand that someone does something because it is a duty or seems reasonable',null,null,'درخواست از کسی که کاری را انجام دهد، زیرا این یک وظیفه است یا معقول به نظر می رسد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['fully expect (= completely ) We fully expected to win.','confidently expect (= with a feeling of confidence ) He confidently expected to be elected again.','half expect (= partly, but not completely ) He walked slowly towards the box, half expecting it to explode.','really expect (= definitely ) I didn’t really expect her to come.','honestly expect (= really expect ) Do you honestly expect me to look after the kids while you go on holiday?','hardly expect (= almost not ) You can hardly expect a child of three to know the difference between right and wrong.','rightly expect (= with good reason ) The public rightly expects government officials to be honest.','as expected (= in the way that was planned or thought likely to happen ) Tickets have not been selling as well as expected.','something is (only) to be expected (= used to say that you are not surprised by something unpleasant ) After all this rain, some flooding is only to be expected.','something happens when you least expect it Bad luck tends to happen when you least expect it.','somebody is entitled to expect something (= have the right to think something will happen ) You’re entitled to expect decent service at these prices.','it is reasonable/unreasonable to expect something It’s unreasonable to expect a tenant to pay for repairs to the outside of the house.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The officer expects complete obedience from his troops.","translation":"افسر از سربازان خود انتظار اطاعت کامل دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001232018.mp3"},{"sentence":"I can’t expect her to be on time if I’m late myself.","translation":"من نمی توانم انتظار داشته باشم که او به موقع بیاید اگر من خودم دیر بیایم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001232021.mp3"},{"sentence":"The school expects a lot of its students.","translation":"مدرسه از دانش آموزان خود انتظار زیادی دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001232025.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('f4162e50-e11f-5643-88e2-401d1ca30855','10b9d129-1b64-5b2f-b399-a5aee9054723',3,'think somebody/something will arrive','فکر کن کسی/چیزی خواهد رسید','spoken & written','to believe that someone or something is going to arrive',null,null,'باور کردن به اینکه کسی یا چیزی قرار است از راه برسد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['fully expect (= completely ) We fully expected to win.','confidently expect (= with a feeling of confidence ) He confidently expected to be elected again.','half expect (= partly, but not completely ) He walked slowly towards the box, half expecting it to explode.','really expect (= definitely ) I didn’t really expect her to come.','honestly expect (= really expect ) Do you honestly expect me to look after the kids while you go on holiday?','hardly expect (= almost not ) You can hardly expect a child of three to know the difference between right and wrong.','rightly expect (= with good reason ) The public rightly expects government officials to be honest.','as expected (= in the way that was planned or thought likely to happen ) Tickets have not been selling as well as expected.','something is (only) to be expected (= used to say that you are not surprised by something unpleasant ) After all this rain, some flooding is only to be expected.','something happens when you least expect it Bad luck tends to happen when you least expect it.','somebody is entitled to expect something (= have the right to think something will happen ) You’re entitled to expect decent service at these prices.','it is reasonable/unreasonable to expect something It’s unreasonable to expect a tenant to pay for repairs to the outside of the house.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We’re expecting Alison home any minute now.","translation":"ما هر لحظه منتظریم آلیسون به خانه برود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001232012.mp3"},{"sentence":"Snow is expected by the weekend.","translation":"تا آخر هفته برف پیش بینی می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001232013.mp3"},{"sentence":"an expected crowd of 80,000 people","translation":"جمعیت مورد انتظار 80000 نفر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653672.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
