('485d74ed-e1b0-57e8-ae53-ec8359cdfa94','fd4f7624-67d7-507b-acc2-a9809110a0e2',6,'arms/legs','بازوها / پاها','spoken & written','to stretch out a hand or leg','[ transitive ]',null,'برای دراز کردن دست یا پا','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"George extended his hand (= offered to shake hands ) .","translation":"جورج دستش را دراز کرد (= پیشنهاد دست دادن را داد).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001657917.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('38b14ed8-db16-5c54-955a-8b9b3a0ee274','fd4f7624-67d7-507b-acc2-a9809110a0e2',7,'continue winning','به برنده شدن ادامه بده','spoken & written','to increase the number of points, games etc by which one person or team is ahead of other competitors','[ transitive ]',null,'برای افزایش تعداد امتیازات، بازی ها و غیره که توسط آن یک فرد یا تیم از سایر رقبا جلوتر است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Manchester United extended their lead at the top of the table to 10 points.","translation":"منچستریونایتد در صدر جدول به 10 امتیاز رسید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001657924.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('ef24fe51-1398-5534-b64d-5400fceed846','fd4f7624-67d7-507b-acc2-a9809110a0e2',8,'furniture','مبلمان','spoken & written','if a table or ladder extends, it can be made longer','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'اگر یک میز یا نردبان گسترش یابد، می توان آن را طولانی تر کرد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('2402e544-4a00-5244-a1e9-0748242c8142','76fd7731-88c7-54b9-a70b-c738f9a21a4d',1,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'to ... extent','حد، میزان؛ دامنه (تأثیر)؛ وسعت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['to some extent/to a certain extent (= partly ) What you say is true to some extent, but it’s not the whole picture.','to a large/great extent (= a large amount ) The materials we use will depend to a large extent on what is available.','to a small extent (= a small amount ) The plan succeeded to a small extent.','to a greater extent (= more ) Children suffer the effects of poor diet to a greater extent than adults.','to a lesser extent ( also to less extent ) (= less ) The same is true for women, though to a lesser extent.','to a considerable/significant extent (= a considerable or significant amount ) The affair affected his popularity to a considerable extent.','to a limited extent (= not a very large amount ) In the USA, and to a limited extent in Britain, the housing market is in recession.','to such an extent that/to the extent that (= so much that ) He annoyed her to such an extent that she had to leave the room.','to the same extent (= to the same amount ) The roads were congested but not to the same extent as in London.','to what extent? (= how much? ) To what extent does cutting down trees contribute to climate change?','the extent to which (= how much ) The report focused on the use of speed cameras, particularly the extent to which they reduced accidents.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('d435c34a-6d8c-56c7-998f-87c2ff806993','76fd7731-88c7-54b9-a70b-c738f9a21a4d',2,null,null,'spoken & written','how large, important, or serious something is, especially something such as a problem or injury','[ uncountable ]',null,'چقدر بزرگ، مهم یا جدی است، به خصوص چیزی مانند یک مشکل یا آسیب','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Considering the extent of his injuries, he’s lucky to be alive.","translation":"با توجه به شدت جراحاتش، او خوش شانس است که زنده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001202143.mp3"},{"sentence":"It’s too early to assess the full extent of the damage.","translation":"هنوز برای ارزیابی میزان کامل خسارت زود است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001627557.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('f1ecd6c3-6054-5232-8039-adca46b5949b','76fd7731-88c7-54b9-a70b-c738f9a21a4d',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the length or size of something','[ uncountable ]',null,'طول یا اندازه چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"They opened out the nets to their full extent .","translation":"آنها تورها را به وسعت خود باز کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001627561.mp3"},{"sentence":"The region is over 10,000 square kilometres in extent.","translation":"این منطقه بیش از 10000 کیلومتر مربع وسعت دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001202138.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('e6e4a4aa-12d5-5f29-a46c-6eb13f645db5','eb337c16-a6a9-55bc-95c3-8d4a1b10b150',1,'cause/influence','علت/تاثیر','spoken & written','one of several things that influence or cause a situation',null,null,'عامل، مؤثر؛ ضریب (عددی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['an important factor Human influence has been an important factor as regards climate change.','a major/minor factor (= the most or least important of several factors ) The country’s huge mineral reserves are a major factor behind its economic strength.','a key/crucial factor (= a very important factor ) A key factor in a company’s success is knowing its customers.','the deciding factor (= the reason for making a particular choice ) The closeness of the river was probably the deciding factor when the site was chosen.','the decisive/determining factor (= the one that has the biggest effect ) The support of middle-income voters was the decisive factor in the election.','a contributing factor (= one that helps to make something happen ) Stress is a contributing factor in many illnesses.','economic factors Economic factors limit our options.','environmental factors Various environmental factors affect the growth of grapes.','social factors Social factors have played their part in the decline in family sizes.','a risk factor (= something that makes you more likely to have an illness ) The highest risk factor for coronary heart disease was found to be smoking.','depend on certain factors Success depends on certain factors.','factors influence something Various factors influenced the government’s decision.','factors determine something The final cost of the product was determined by a combination of factors.','factors are responsible for something These underlying factors were responsible for his death.','a combination/variety/number of factors A combination of factors led to the closure of the factory.','take certain factors into account (= to consider factors when making a decision ) You should take all these factors into account.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The rise in crime is mainly due to social and economic factors.","translation":"افزایش جرایم عمدتاً ناشی از عوامل اجتماعی و اقتصادی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001206740.mp3"},{"sentence":"The vaccination program has been a major factor in the improvement of health standards.","translation":"برنامه واکسیناسیون عامل اصلی در بهبود استانداردهای بهداشتی بوده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001206743.mp3"},{"sentence":"The weather could be a crucial factor in tomorrow’s game.","translation":"آب و هوا می تواند یک عامل تعیین کننده در بازی فردا باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001206746.mp3"},{"sentence":"We liked both houses, but price was the deciding factor.","translation":"ما هر دو خانه را دوست داشتیم، اما قیمت عامل تعیین کننده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001206750.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('6d1fcdb0-b312-52f8-8c74-ada436d10534','eb337c16-a6a9-55bc-95c3-8d4a1b10b150',2,'level on a scale','سطح در یک مقیاس','spoken & written','a particular level on a scale that measures how strong or effective something is',null,null,'سطح خاصی در مقیاسی که میزان قوی یا مؤثر بودن چیزی را می سنجد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['an important factor Human influence has been an important factor as regards climate change.','a major/minor factor (= the most or least important of several factors ) The country’s huge mineral reserves are a major factor behind its economic strength.','a key/crucial factor (= a very important factor ) A key factor in a company’s success is knowing its customers.','the deciding factor (= the reason for making a particular choice ) The closeness of the river was probably the deciding factor when the site was chosen.','the decisive/determining factor (= the one that has the biggest effect ) The support of middle-income voters was the decisive factor in the election.','a contributing factor (= one that helps to make something happen ) Stress is a contributing factor in many illnesses.','economic factors Economic factors limit our options.','environmental factors Various environmental factors affect the growth of grapes.','social factors Social factors have played their part in the decline in family sizes.','a risk factor (= something that makes you more likely to have an illness ) The highest risk factor for coronary heart disease was found to be smoking.','depend on certain factors Success depends on certain factors.','factors influence something Various factors influenced the government’s decision.','factors determine something The final cost of the product was determined by a combination of factors.','factors are responsible for something These underlying factors were responsible for his death.','a combination/variety/number of factors A combination of factors led to the closure of the factory.','take certain factors into account (= to consider factors when making a decision ) You should take all these factors into account.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"factor 15 suntan oil","translation":"روغن برنزه فاکتور 15","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001206760.mp3"},{"sentence":"Even in July the wind chill factor (= the degree to which the air feels colder because of the wind ) can be intense.","translation":"حتی در ماه جولای، ضریب سرمای باد (= درجه ای که هوا به دلیل باد سردتر می شود) می تواند شدید باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001206761.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
