('dc888129-ae51-5cda-a8f2-cb9aebc48be1','b363d1e9-2286-543e-b2f2-2a44f8fa3af9',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to divide a number into factors',null,null,'برای تقسیم یک عدد به فاکتورها','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('55604f4e-262d-5bce-977a-adfcb5d86803','2eeb62eb-9fe3-50d5-9c61-42f591f12f80',1,null,null,'spoken & written','more than a little, but much less than very','[ +adj/adverb ]',null,'نسبتاً، تا حدی؛ کاملاً (به معنای کمتر از خیلی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The house had a fairly large garden.","translation":"خانه یک باغ نسبتا بزرگ داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001209194.mp3"},{"sentence":"She speaks English fairly well.","translation":"او انگلیسی را نسبتاً خوب صحبت می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001209195.mp3"},{"sentence":"The instructions seem fairly straightforward.","translation":"دستورالعمل ها نسبتاً ساده به نظر می رسند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001647685.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('01f9af04-04ff-55be-8b5e-5b77b688dbeb','2eeb62eb-9fe3-50d5-9c61-42f591f12f80',2,null,null,'spoken & written','in a way that is fair , honest , and reasonable',null,null,'به گونه ای که منصفانه، صادقانه و معقول باشد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I felt I hadn’t been treated fairly.","translation":"احساس کردم با من عادلانه رفتار نشده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001209204.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('18fde05f-0bec-5bc7-8f03-863814e4ca1b','2eeb62eb-9fe3-50d5-9c61-42f591f12f80',3,null,null,'old-fashioned','used to emphasize the degree , force etc of an action',null,null,'برای تأکید بر درجه، نیرو و غیره یک عمل استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He fairly raced past us on his bike.","translation":"او نسبتاً با دوچرخه اش از کنار ما گذشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001209210.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('a9952947-a183-5d84-8e16-462b2c31660a','00afaf12-1bed-5189-bf0a-a8a14d1dcb61',1,'closely related group','گروه نزدیک به هم','spoken & written','a group of people who are related to each other, especially a mother , a father , and their children','[ countable ]',null,'خانواده، خویشاوندان؛ رده (زیست‌شناسی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the whole family We invited the whole family round.','all the family This is a game which all the family can enjoy.','somebody''s immediate family (= closest relations ) What if one of your immediate family were disabled?','somebody''s extended family (= including not only parents and children, but also grandparents, aunts etc ) She gets a lot of help from her extended family.','a large/small family She came from a large family of seven children.','a one-parent/single-parent family One in seven families is a one-parent family.','the nuclear family (= a family consisting of a mother, a father, and their children ) Not everyone lives in a typical nuclear family.','close/close-knit family (= a family that spends a lot of time together and gives each other support ) Laura''s family are very close.','the Royal family (= the king or queen and their family ) The Royal Family have large estates in Scotland.','the Smith/Jones/Brown etc family The Smith family are living in temporary accommodation.','a family member/a member of the family The event was attended by many of his family members, including his children and grandchildren.','somebody''s family background He comes from a stable family background.','a family history Is there a family history of heart disease?','family life Some people believe that television is destroying family life.','a family unit the breakup of the traditional family unit','somebody''s family home (= where someone''s family live and where they lived as a child ) Her family home is in a village outside Derry.','a family business (= one run by members of a family ) My parents expected me to join the family business.','a family car (= one designed for families with children ) It''s a practical family car that is also fun to drive.','a family holiday British English , a family vacation American English: Most of our family holidays were spent in the south of France.','a family resemblance (= when members of the same family look like each other ) There''s a strong family resemblance between all the sisters.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Do you know the family next door?","translation":"آیا خانواده همسایه را می شناسید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001211075.mp3"},{"sentence":"The Webb family still has its farm over there.","translation":"خانواده وب هنوز مزرعه خود را در آنجا دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001647903.mp3"},{"sentence":"This house isn’t big enough for a family of seven.","translation":"این خانه به اندازه کافی برای یک خانواده هفت نفره بزرگ نیست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001970214.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('b94058be-1bd2-55c2-b4bb-3ae2b6bdbc68','00afaf12-1bed-5189-bf0a-a8a14d1dcb61',2,'all your relations','تمام روابط شما','spoken & written','all the people you are related to, including those who are now dead','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'تمام افرادی که با آنها خویشاوند هستید، از جمله کسانی که اکنون مرده اند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the whole family We invited the whole family round.','all the family This is a game which all the family can enjoy.','somebody''s immediate family (= closest relations ) What if one of your immediate family were disabled?','somebody''s extended family (= including not only parents and children, but also grandparents, aunts etc ) She gets a lot of help from her extended family.','a large/small family She came from a large family of seven children.','a one-parent/single-parent family One in seven families is a one-parent family.','the nuclear family (= a family consisting of a mother, a father, and their children ) Not everyone lives in a typical nuclear family.','close/close-knit family (= a family that spends a lot of time together and gives each other support ) Laura''s family are very close.','the Royal family (= the king or queen and their family ) The Royal Family have large estates in Scotland.','the Smith/Jones/Brown etc family The Smith family are living in temporary accommodation.','a family member/a member of the family The event was attended by many of his family members, including his children and grandchildren.','somebody''s family background He comes from a stable family background.','a family history Is there a family history of heart disease?','family life Some people believe that television is destroying family life.','a family unit the breakup of the traditional family unit','somebody''s family home (= where someone''s family live and where they lived as a child ) Her family home is in a village outside Derry.','a family business (= one run by members of a family ) My parents expected me to join the family business.','a family car (= one designed for families with children ) It''s a practical family car that is also fun to drive.','a family holiday British English , a family vacation American English: Most of our family holidays were spent in the south of France.','a family resemblance (= when members of the same family look like each other ) There''s a strong family resemblance between all the sisters.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I’m moving to Detroit because I have some family there.","translation":"من به دیترویت نقل مکان می کنم زیرا خانواده ای در آنجا دارم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001211104.mp3"},{"sentence":"That painting has been in our family (= been owned by our family ) for 200 years.","translation":"آن نقاشی 200 سال است که در خانواده ما (= متعلق به خانواده ما) بوده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001211111.mp3"},{"sentence":"Asthma runs in the family (= is common in the family ) .","translation":"آسم در خانواده شایع است (= در خانواده شایع است).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001211115.mp3"},{"sentence":"The family now lives in London.","translation":"این خانواده اکنون در لندن زندگی می کنند.","audio_url":null},{"sentence":"My family comes from Scotland originally.","translation":"خانواده من در اصل اهل اسکاتلند هستند.","audio_url":null},{"sentence":"The family now live in London.","translation":"این خانواده اکنون در لندن زندگی می کنند.","audio_url":null},{"sentence":"My family come from Scotland originally.","translation":"خانواده من در اصل اهل اسکاتلند هستند.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,7),
('d77cd281-1375-5cdc-ba60-dd6b5c79d0e3','00afaf12-1bed-5189-bf0a-a8a14d1dcb61',3,'children','کودکان','spoken & written','children','[ countable ]',null,'کودکان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Couples with young families wouldn’t want to live here.","translation":"زوج‌هایی که خانواده‌های جوانی دارند، نمی‌خواهند اینجا زندگی کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001211122.mp3"},{"sentence":"They’re getting married next year, and hope to start a family (= have children ) straight away.","translation":"آنها سال آینده ازدواج می کنند و امیدوارند که فوراً یک خانواده (= بچه دار شوند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001211126.mp3"},{"sentence":"the problems of bringing up a family on a very low income","translation":"مشکلات تشکیل خانواده با درآمد بسیار کم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001211129.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
