('bdb5bf19-bb06-5016-9c15-4f9575fd17ff','427e9671-4472-5436-89b2-ed407d1b42bd',1,null,null,'spoken & written','likely to happen or exist at a time after the present',null,null,'آینده، پیش‌رو (زمان)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We are now more able to predict future patterns of climate change.","translation":"ما اکنون قادر به پیش بینی الگوهای آینده تغییرات آب و هوایی هستیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001317278.mp3"},{"sentence":"We’ve been able to save this land from development and preserve it for future generations .","translation":"ما توانسته ایم این سرزمین را از توسعه نجات دهیم و برای نسل های آینده حفظ کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001725567.mp3"},{"sentence":"the debate over the future development of the European Union","translation":"بحث در مورد توسعه آینده اتحادیه اروپا","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001824358.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('03b244ad-23c7-5ed2-a404-b4d64379e6e1','427e9671-4472-5436-89b2-ed407d1b42bd',2,null,null,'technical','the form of a verb used for talking about things that are going to happen',null,null,'شکل یک فعل که برای صحبت در مورد چیزهایی که قرار است اتفاق بیفتد استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the future tense","translation":"زمان آینده","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001317286.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('0769143d-66ae-5e42-914e-950a7ad8d93e','427e9671-4472-5436-89b2-ed407d1b42bd',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'for future reference','آینده، پیش‌رو (زمان)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('e7970b82-87ac-5fd2-9371-7a98da6e8959','fb35abb3-2632-5387-8165-406a4629e273',1,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'the future','آینده، آینده‌نگری؛ آینده (کار)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['predict the future (= say what will happen in the future ) No-one can predict the future of boxing.','foretell the future (= say or show what will happen in the future ) Some people think that dreams can foretell the future.','see/look into the future (= know what will happen in the future ) I wish I could see into the future.','look to the future (= think about or plan for the future ) She could now look to the future with confidence.','plan for the future ( also make plans for the future ) (= think carefully about the future and decide what you are going to do ) As soon as she knew she was pregnant, she started to plan for the future.','face a bleak/grim etc future Many pensioners face a bleak future.','shape somebody''s future Your boss is the one who writes your evaluations, recommends you for promotions and shapes your future.','somebody’s/something’s future lies in/with something (= it is in a particular thing ) The country’s economic future lies with its skilled workforce.','the future looks good/bright etc The future looks good for the company.','great/good The country has a great future.','bright/promising (= showing signs of being successful ) Her future as a tennis player looks promising.','uncertain (= not clear or decided ) The college''s future is now uncertain.','bleak/grim/dark (= without anything to make you feel hopeful ) The theatre is losing money and its future looks bleak.','the immediate future (= very soon ) There will be no major changes in the immediate future.','the near future (= soon ) A new product launch is planned for the near future.','the distant future (= a long time from now ) I don''t worry about what might happen in the distant future.','the dim and distant future (= a very long time from now ) He plans to get married in the dim and distant future.','for/in the foreseeable future (= as far into the future as you can possibly know ) The population is expected to keep growing for the foreseeable future.','in the not too distant future (= quite soon ) We’re planning to go there again in the not too distant future.','somebody’s hopes/fears/plans for the future What are your hopes for the future?','somebody’s worries/concerns about the future their worries about the future of the English countryside','what the future holds (= what will happen ) He is worried about what the future holds for the company.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('f4777ed0-8658-5788-8105-0b1be70afc75','fb35abb3-2632-5387-8165-406a4629e273',2,null,null,'spoken & written','what someone or something will do or what will happen to them in the future','[ countable ]',null,'چه کسی یا چیزی انجام خواهد داد یا در آینده چه اتفاقی برای آنها خواهد افتاد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['predict the future (= say what will happen in the future ) No-one can predict the future of boxing.','foretell the future (= say or show what will happen in the future ) Some people think that dreams can foretell the future.','see/look into the future (= know what will happen in the future ) I wish I could see into the future.','look to the future (= think about or plan for the future ) She could now look to the future with confidence.','plan for the future ( also make plans for the future ) (= think carefully about the future and decide what you are going to do ) As soon as she knew she was pregnant, she started to plan for the future.','face a bleak/grim etc future Many pensioners face a bleak future.','shape somebody''s future Your boss is the one who writes your evaluations, recommends you for promotions and shapes your future.','somebody’s/something’s future lies in/with something (= it is in a particular thing ) The country’s economic future lies with its skilled workforce.','the future looks good/bright etc The future looks good for the company.','great/good The country has a great future.','bright/promising (= showing signs of being successful ) Her future as a tennis player looks promising.','uncertain (= not clear or decided ) The college''s future is now uncertain.','bleak/grim/dark (= without anything to make you feel hopeful ) The theatre is losing money and its future looks bleak.','the immediate future (= very soon ) There will be no major changes in the immediate future.','the near future (= soon ) A new product launch is planned for the near future.','the distant future (= a long time from now ) I don''t worry about what might happen in the distant future.','the dim and distant future (= a very long time from now ) He plans to get married in the dim and distant future.','for/in the foreseeable future (= as far into the future as you can possibly know ) The population is expected to keep growing for the foreseeable future.','in the not too distant future (= quite soon ) We’re planning to go there again in the not too distant future.','somebody’s hopes/fears/plans for the future What are your hopes for the future?','somebody’s worries/concerns about the future their worries about the future of the English countryside','what the future holds (= what will happen ) He is worried about what the future holds for the company.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The islands should have the right to decide their own future.","translation":"جزایر باید حق تصمیم گیری درباره آینده خود را داشته باشند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001317334.mp3"},{"sentence":"Ferguson is optimistic about the future of the business.","translation":"فرگوسن نسبت به آینده کسب و کار خوشبین است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001725594.mp3"},{"sentence":"a leader who will shape the organization’s future","translation":"رهبری که آینده سازمان را شکل خواهد داد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001970986.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
